eed to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}-3x+4\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-3x+4 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}+3x-4) & =0 \\\\ -(x+4)(x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=1,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6a5528147c994e180c2ffb41bd259dae489a3fc02fa1d6c77452d6cf1722e9be.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-4$ or $x>1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75991/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75991"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70303/selection/caa3a3fed786a86648392a86978b50fbfc897f9a7d3189054ed9f28513b05fe7" :answer/id #uuid "12b117f9-be8d-5233-a413-1b4992519d05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3<x<3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70303/selection/db17c90d5d2fac9165fb64affbc4618a76285cb7400a1e85b7e1ee51a2593fcf" :answer/id #uuid "5ddfafa3-cab3-5c67-b75a-b93000be8163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x<3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70303/selection/ed8ac9de55115bf529f403a3b053851c90105af69cafabfb193ca7589490c79a" :answer/id #uuid "248e656b-e729-508a-858e-603a397ae85a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x<0$ or $x>3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70303/selection/3d737f6d6da4c78e32390603dbf65e4e0bd349f86da09a9470aab088d4dfb724" :answer/id #uuid "5ff80692-da9c-5a78-96fd-857b3061bfec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x<-3$ or $x>1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70303/selection/4f5c9f616ea0c33db56870e626d576a78beac04899ec339627e265a11f4c8ba8" :answ