 and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/a341979142ef569d7ba4ec5b44178e8b4e4374fa9294e4664ae0f0008b76caab.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-3x<0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0<x<3.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (0,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-3878/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3878"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277671/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "c85749d4-d1f2-5db6-98ee-f36b3d2c06ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277671/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2c404b6a-96c5-5345-b717-148acadd2c70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277671/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "472af46d-1570-5103-b2d3-1862fb2b88cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277671/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-277671/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-277671/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277671/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "aaad5350-323d-5306-93ad-8cd509b20e91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277671/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "feb82d6e-411e-56d8-a96e-bd0990c0cebe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277671/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-277671/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277671" :question/id #uuid "0f81b704-2a60-5224-96b8-0941c805eb95" :question/math-academy-id "q-277671" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-2{x}^{2}>10x+12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2} & >10x+12 \\\\ -2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-10x-12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+10x+12 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+6x)+(4x+12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+3)+4(x+3) & =0 \\\\ (2x+4)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=-2,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/539e0e68f4a03c0bd4a309ebf2c4a00638d99c6eee233ca8f2cef3814e419c95.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-10x-12>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-3<x<-2.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-3,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-277671/field-1" "q-277671/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/vali