4f97a4e948b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142177" :question/id #uuid "292302ac-904d-59fe-b02a-d8afa13eb915" :question/math-academy-id "q-142177" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-5{x}^{2}>10x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{x}^{2} & >10x \\\\ -5{x}^{2}-10x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-5{x}^{2}-10x$ lies above the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{x}^{2}-10x & =0 \\\\ -5x(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=-2,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/6cb044d4c6280d77dd525f6e2a8702d9fcba1553c2d33411407d69e09a6b715b.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-5{x}^{2}-10x>0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2<x<0.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-2,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142177/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142177"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277664/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer/id #uuid "3fbfbae5-eba9-5a3f-b48b-83a9c663c33f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277664/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8f440c1d-110c-54ac-84b4-2a40cd3598f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277664/field-1" :answer-